# ACT II — the voyage
room marrow_deck "The Marrow — Main Deck"
  bg bg_deck_wide
  width 2560
  music music_sea
  ambience sea
  perspective horizon 230 ref 875 height 330
  # The quarterdeck stairs and their banisters fill x≈1340–1880; they are an exit, not floor.
  walk (80,875) (110,706) (1320,706) (1320,875)
  entry 780,805
  arrive marrow_quarterdeck 1250,820
  arrive below_decks 955,790
  arrive bow_fog 820,710
  arrive crows_nest 660,720

  # Atmosphere: sun on the sea past the rail, and the ship talking to herself.
  footsteps deck
  motes glints (1410,385) (1650,385) (1650,500) (1415,500) count 18
  emit creak

  sprite npc_quill_body at 560,800 size 0.98 idle speaker quill for quill grade "saturate(0.85) brightness(0.92)"
  sprite prop_spyglass at 300,838 size 0.24 for spyglass

  hotspot rail "the sea"
    area 1000,330 600x190
    nowalk
    look "Open water, going gold at the edge. Three years I watched from the quay. It looks the same from here. Either comfort or insult."
    talk "I say good morning to the sea. It has heard better."
    use "The compass says the Straits are that way. The sea says nothing at all."

  hotspot forward "the foredeck"
    area 560,320 430x230
    stand 820,710
    look "The foredeck and the bow. Fog sits on the water ahead like a hen on an egg. The Marrow steers politely round it."
    open "Hobb has roped off the bow until the captain says otherwise. The rope has a knot in it that looks like an opinion."
    walk "Hobb's rope across the foredeck says no. So, in fairness, does Hobb."
    state if vane_convinced
      exit bow_fog sound none
      look "The foredeck, and past it the bow, already half gone in the fog. That's my post."
      open "I go forward, into the fog."

  hotspot shrouds "the shrouds"
    area 470,0 200x330
    stand 660,720
    look "The shrouds: rope ladders up to the crow's nest. Lookout's territory. I'd get two rungs up before Quill had me down by the collar."
    use "Not yet. Up there is for crew who know where they're looking."
    pickup "They're attached to the mast. Firmly. That's rather the point of them."
    state if quill_navigator
      look "The shrouds, rung by rope rung up to the crow's nest. Quill keeps the night watch on the deck now."
      use "I wait for dark and climb. Quill lets me reach the second ratline, then fetches me down. We keep watch at the foot of the mast."
        go crows_nest sound none
      open: go crows_nest sound none

  hotspot crates "lashed crates"
    area 200,340 400x300
    stand 420,760
    look "Crates lashed for sea. Someone stencilled QUARANTINE STN, G.K. on them, then painted a cloud over it. Badly. The mark mattered."
    open "The lids are nailed. Somebody wanted them to stay shut. I may have a tool for that."
    state if kelp_seen
      look "Kelp briquettes for a quarantine station, sealed with Cray's cloud. Who ships smoke? And who needs that much of it?"
      open "I've seen inside one. That was plenty."

  hotspot hatch "hatch to below decks"
    area 790,805 330x75
    stand 955,790
    exit below_decks sound hatch
    look "The main hatch, propped open. A smell of tar and hammocks comes up, and something that wants very badly to be stew."
    open "I go below. The ladder is steeper than it looks, and it looks steep."

  hotspot quill "Quill"
    show if not quill_navigator
    area 500,505 110x300
    stand 760,805
    look "Quill, the lookout, back to the rail, eyes on me and not the horizon. She stands like someone guarding a door that isn't there."
    talk "She's already looking. I get the feeling she's been looking for a while."
      talk quill
    give "She doesn't take things from cargo."

  hotspot spyglass "spyglass"
    show if not has spyglass and not quill_helped
    area 240,780 140x80
    stand 420,810
    item spyglass
    look "A brass spyglass, wedged between two crates where the sea put it. Dented twice."
    pickup "I pocket the spyglass. Somebody on this deck is missing it badly."

  hotspot stairs_up "quarterdeck steps"
    show if quill_helped = true
    area 1340,520 540x340
    stand 1290,820
    exit marrow_quarterdeck sound stairs
    look "The steps up to the quarterdeck. Nobody's stopping me now."
    open "I go up."

  hotspot stairs_blocked "quarterdeck steps"
    show if not quill_helped
    area 1340,520 540x340
    stand 1290,820
    look "The steps up to the quarterdeck. Quill is standing where the rail meets them, which is not an accident."
    open "Quill puts a hand on the rail. “Crew aft of the mast. You're not crew.”"
    use "Not while she's standing there, I'm not."
    walk "Quill shakes her head before I've taken a step."

  use crowbar on crates if not kelp_seen
    "I lever up a lid. No cargo: dried kelp, pressed into bricks, each stamped with Cray's cloud. Who ships smoke? I nail it back."
    set kelp_seen
    sound pickup
  use crowbar on crates
    "Once was enough. The kelp isn't going to explain itself a second time."
  use spyglass on quill if not quill_helped
    "I hold out the spyglass. Quill's hand closes on it before I've finished. Then, remembering herself, she doesn't pull."
    talk quill at lost
  use sextant on quill if vane_terms
    "I hold out Pell's sextant. Quill looks at it, and then at me, and doesn't take it straight away."
    talk quill at sextant
  use sextant on quill
    "She turns it over and hands it back. “Pell's. Navigate what? The captain's going the long way, and the long way steers itself.”"
  use manifest on quill
    "She skims it. “Twenty-two names and a navigator who wasn't drowned. Show it to someone who's lost somebody. Not me.”"
  use pell_log on quill
    "She won't open it. “That's the captain's to read. Pell would've said so, if he'd finished saying things.”"
  use licence on quill
    "She reads it without taking it. “Says you can sail. Doesn't say you can get past me. Different department.”"
  use compass on rail
    "The needle swings off north and settles on the horizon. It has heard its name."
  use spyglass on rail
    "I put the spyglass to my eye. The sea, closer. It's no less enormous. It's just enormous in more detail."
